B.QL=s(["What does this app actually do?","It works out how to spread your TSP contributions across the year so you finish it the way you meant to \u2014 reaching the annual limit if that is your aim, without running into it early and losing months of matching. It reads your pay, your election and what you have already contributed, and tells you the percentage to enter in MyPay."],t.s)
B.VT=s(["Where do the numbers come from?","Pay tables, contribution limits and allowance figures are transcribed from the official published sources and carried in the app as dated files with their citations. Nothing is estimated and nothing is worked out from a rule of thumb. If the app does not have a figure it says so rather than guessing one."],t.s)
B.OM=s(["Does anything I enter leave my device?","No. Nothing about you leaves your device. There are no accounts, nothing to sign in to, and nothing the app reports back. Reading a statement happens right here, including the picture or PDF itself. If you are using the app in a browser, your browser downloads the app the same way it downloads any web page \u2014 that is the only thing that crosses the internet, and it carries nothing about you. The pay tables the app works from are built in, which is why a new year's figures arrive with a new version of the app."],t.s)
B.Qt=s(["Why does it ask for a statement?","A statement carries the facts the plan needs \u2014 your pay, your current election, and what you have contributed so far this year \u2014 and reading them is faster and more accurate than typing them. You never have to: everything can be entered by hand, and you can correct anything the app reads."],t.s)
B.V2=s(["What do I do with the percentage it gives me?","Enter it in MyPay as your TSP contribution election. The app shows the figure for each remaining month, because a plan that gets you to the limit usually changes at least once during the year."],t.s)
B.S9=s(["Why did my plan change after I entered a month?","Because the plan is worked out from where you actually are, not from where you expected to be. A month that came in higher or lower than planned changes what the remaining months have to do. That is the app working, not the app being inconsistent."],t.s)
B.TG=s(["Is this official?","No. This is not a government application and it is not affiliated with DFAS, the TSP or any branch of service. It is a planning tool. Your statement, MyPay and the TSP are the record; if they disagree with this app, they are right."],t.s)
B.Rd=s(["Something looks wrong. What do I do?","Send feedback from the More menu and say what you saw. It also helps to check the pay year shown on the plan, since a plan built for last year against this year of pay will look wrong in exactly the way you would expect."],t.s)
